 {
  "id": 867905,
  "url": "https://freesound.org/people/inspire153/sounds/867905/",
  "name": "Wood ants walking along a trail",
  "tags": [
   "Formica",
   "ant",
   "ants",
   "field",
   "footsteps",
   "forest",
   "insect",
   "insects",
   "nature",
   "recording",
   "stereo",
   "trail",
   "walking",
   "wildlife",
   "wood"
  ],
  "description": "Wood ants walking along a trail\n\nI was curious whether the very quiet sounds of wood ants (Formica sp.) could be recorded with a conventional stereo microphone without placing the microphone directly on the nest or disturbing the ants.\n\nThis recording was made on 26 August 2026 on a sunny, calm day. A Schoeps MSTC 74 stereo microphone was positioned low above the ground, directly beside a busy ant trail leading between the nest and a nearby maple tree. The microphone was not placed on the nest and the ants were not allowed onto the microphone.\n\nI was genuinely surprised by how clearly the continuous movement of the ants was captured. This was my first attempt at recording them, and I had expected the result to be much quieter.\n\nRecorded in Estonia.\n\nVideo link\n<a href=\"https://youtu.be/ANQR0p1VRsM\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://youtu.be/ANQR0p1VRsM</a>",
  "license": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",
  "type": "wav",
  "duration": 27.3019,
  "samplerate": 48000.0,
  "username": "inspire153",
