 {
  "id": 868204,
  "url": "https://freesound.org/people/inspire153/sounds/868204/",
  "name": "Recording wood ants with two shotgun microphones. ISO track captured with the Schoeps MiniCMIT GR",
  "tags": [
   "Formica",
   "anttrail",
   "biologicalsounds",
   "insects",
   "microsounds",
   "woodants"
  ],
  "description": "Recording wood ants with two shotgun microphones\nA field‑recording experiment to capture the extremely quiet sounds of wood ants (Formica sp.) moving along a busy trail.\n\nFor this test I used two shotgun microphones aimed at approximately the same area but positioned at different distances: a Schoeps MiniCMIT GR closer to the ant trail and a DPA 2017 Shotgun Microphone placed farther away.\n\nSeveral recordings were made, including a clean version without NoiseAssist and additional takes using NoiseAssist at −10 dB on both microphone channels. Interestingly, the noise reduction allowed me to raise the input gain significantly without introducing noticeable distortion.\n\nIn addition to the main stereo recordings, I have included a single ISO track captured with the Schoeps MiniCMIT GR positioned closest to the trail.\n\nThe ants were not deliberately disturbed, and the microphones were positioned so that they could not reach or climb onto the equipment.\n\nRecorded in Estonia, August 2026.\n\nVideo link\n<a href=\"https://youtu.be/Hw8zdzfWrc0\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://youtu.be/Hw8zdzfWrc0</a>",
  "license": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",
  "type": "wav",
  "duration": 68.5839,
  "samplerate": 48000.0,
  "username": "inspire153",
